ermediate"><addressbook><name>BABA, SHUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJINO, KENTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOJO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A high-modulus rubber composition and pneumatic tire which are obtained efficiently. The composition comprises a rubber component comprising at least either of natural rubber and a synthetic diene rubber, at least one maleimide compound, and at least one nitrogen compound selected from the group consisting of polyaniline, hydrazides, and amine compounds.  It is used as a tread material.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition caoutchoutée à module élevé et un pneumatique produits de manière efficace. Cette composition renferme un constituant caoutchouté comprenant au moins du caoutchouc naturel et un caoutchouc diénique synthétique, au moins un composé de maléimide, et au moins un composé azoté choisi dans le groupe formé par la polyaniline, les hydrazides, et les composés aminés. Cette composition caoutchoutée est destinée à être utilisée pour former une semelle.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>